<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Bengal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> is a state in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Kolkata</a> as its capital, stretching from the Himalayan foothills at Darjeeling to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>. It was created at the partition of 1947, when the western, largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> part of the Bengal Province joined India and the eastern part became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-pakistan">East Pakistan</a>, later Bangladesh. It is one of India's most populous states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-bengal.jpg" alt="West Bengal" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shubhankar.sengupta19 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Howrah_bridge_betwixt_Lights.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
